      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The long-term follow-up (LTFU) team at the Seattle Cancer Care Alliance uses telemedicine to diagnose and treat post-transplantation complications in hematopoietic cell transplantation (HCT) survivors. Photos are often requested via the telemedicine service to aid in diagnosis, but they are typically of poor quality, making them unusable."
        },
        {
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "This project offered bachelor of science in nursing students, partnered with a comprehensive cancer center, the opportunity to participate in an evidence-based practice project to improve detection and management of chronic graft-versus-host disease (cGVHD) in patients after HCT."
        },
        {
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Students partnered with RNs to develop instructional tools using multiple evidence sources. A brochure and video were developed."
        },
        {
          "Label": "FINDINGS",
          "content": "Providing these instructional tools to those in the LTFU program improved patient outcomes for managing cGVHD through telemedicine. This partnership provided an opportunity for mutual learning and improved clinical practice."
        }
      ]},
